From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:43:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] dmaengine: imx-dma: bring back i.MX21 support

Commit 39dc2a4929f7 ("dmaengine: imx-dma: Remove i.MX21 support")
removed the i.MX21 match. Restore it: the i.MX21 DMA is the i.MX27's
without hardware chaining, which is all IMX21_DMA changes. The binding
still lists fsl,imx21-dma.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1fN5Ee1gRFAS7tp8oLbvQ
---
 drivers/dma/imx-dma.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/dma/imx-dma.c b/drivers/dma/imx-dma.c
index 81c627643..45b758500 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/imx-dma.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/imx-dma.c
@@ -168,6 +168,7 @@ struct imxdma_channel {
 
 enum imx_dma_type {
 	IMX1_DMA,
+	IMX21_DMA,
 	IMX27_DMA,
 };
 
@@ -194,6 +195,8 @@ struct imxdma_filter_data {
 static const struct of_device_id imx_dma_of_dev_id[] = {
 	{
 		.compatible = "fsl,imx1-dma", .data = (const void *)IMX1_DMA,
+	}, {
+		.compatible = "fsl,imx21-dma", .data = (const void *)IMX21_DMA,
 	}, {
 		.compatible = "fsl,imx27-dma", .data = (const void *)IMX27_DMA,
 	}, {
